- Item 3 (optional): Quotation builder Phase 3 — column reordering UI + save/load named
  markup-column templates. T2 ~15-20K.

## New recurring-pattern lessons surfaced during Batch 15 (apply at Batch 16 PRE-FLIGHT):

- Public route + protected tRPC procedure = mismatch. New pre-flight item 9 (above)
  catches this. When in doubt: direct Prisma in the Server Component with an explicit
  visibility filter (e.g. `isActive=true AND ecommerceVisible=true` for products).

- RED → GREEN with explicit vitest run between steps. Cost: one extra vitest run per
  batch (~2s). Benefit: provable assertion-mismatch errors before implementation;
  catches accidentally-already-passing tests (regression-guard role). Continue this
  pattern in every batch with new tests.

- Squash-merge requires `git branch -D`, not `-d`. The squash workflow doesn't update
  the merge graph from the source branch's tip, so `-d` rejects the delete as "not
  fully merged". Always use `-D` post-squash-merge — this is by design, not a force-
  delete of unmerged work.

- `Array.isArray` narrows to `any[]` under strict TS. Cast to `unknown[]` after the
  guard before accessing elements: `if (Array.isArray(x)) { const arr = x as unknown[]; ... }`.

- Native `<img>` is acceptable in a Server Component when next/image isn't already
  configured for the route. Don't add bogus eslint-disable comments for rules not in
  the project's lint config. Defer next/image migration until there's a perf reason.

- vercel-plugin skill hooks (next-forge, next-cache-components, nextjs, react-best-practices)
  auto-fire on file path / import patterns. Per Rule 28 priority order these never override
  CLAUDE.md conventions. Acknowledge once + continue — project locks self-hosted Postgres
  via Docker Compose + `dynamic = "force-dynamic"` Server Components across 10+ pages.

